  {
   "t": 70.72,
   "kind": "thought",
   "data": {
    "text": "In a `120 mm / 3 h` storm over the whole `lagos-lekki-v2` area:\n\n### 1. Baseline - no interventions\n\nRun `r_a9cb390eab1dd07f` - preset `baseline 120mm/3h` verbatim, defaults for pattern / hours:\n\nWhole study area:\n\n* `buildings_flooded` 29137, `buildings_flooded_severe` 8230\n* `road_km_impassable` 384.7 km, threshold 0.3 m\n* `people_exposed` 88124\n* `flooded_area_km2` 21.8598, `max_depth_m` 2.051\n\nInside `Lekki-Epe Expressway` corridor:\n\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:road_km_impassable` 34.912 km\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:max_depth_m` 1.142 m\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:flooded_area_km2` 0.7805\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:buildings_flooded` 731\n\nExpressway is impassable.\n\nScreened combinations with `surrogate_sweep` for `objective road_km_impassable`. Screening only - not cited. Top prediction was city-wide new drainage. Confirmed one change at a time with the solver.\n\n### 2. 1 intervention: city-wide new drainage 40 mm/h\n\nRun `r_af9b605766635798` :\n\n`drain_upgrade add_mm_h 40` with no `place` = city-wide new drainage, not a local fix.\n\nWhole area vs baseline `r_a9cb390eab1dd07f`:\n\n* `buildings_flooded` 10107 vs 29137\n* `buildings_flooded_severe` 24 vs 8230\n* `road_km_impassable` 15.164 vs 384.7 : delta -369.536 km\n* `people_exposed` 15142 vs 88124\n* `max_depth_m` 0.599 vs 2.051\n\nInside `Lekki-Epe Expressway`:\n\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:road_km_impassable` 1.091 km vs 34.912 km baseline - ~97% reduction\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:max_depth_m` 0.405 m vs 1.142 m - still > 0.3 m threshold\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:flooded_area_km2` 0.1274 vs 0.7805\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:buildings_flooded` 231 vs 731\n\nBiggest single-step benefit, but not 0 km impassable.\n\n### 3. 2 interventions: city-wide existing drains x3 + city-wide new 40 mm/h\n\nRun `r_62388ceb325c1052` :\n\n```\ndrain_upgrade capacity_factor 3.0 + add_mm_h 40.0, whole area\n```\n\nInside `Lekki-Epe Expressway`:\n\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:road_km_impassable` 0.617 km\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:max_depth_m` 0.405 m\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:flooded_area_km2` 0.0821\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:buildings_flooded` 180\n\nWhole area `road_km_impassable` 14.015 km, `buildings_flooded` 9746.\n\nHalves the remaining expressway gap from 1.091 km to 0.617 km.\n\n### 4. 3 interventions: add green in Lekki Phase 1\n\nRun `r_c2aa593db6d235e6` :\n\n```\ndrain_upgrade capacity_factor 3.0 + add_mm_h 40.0 whole area\n+ green place Lekki Phase 1 infiltration 40 mm/h\n```\n\nInside `Lekki-Epe Expressway`:\n\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:road_km_impassable` 0.617 km - no change vs 2-intervention set\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:max_depth_m` 0.405 m - no change\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:flooded_area_km2` 0.0764 vs 0.0821\n* `area:Lekki-Epe Expressway:buildings_flooded` 176 vs 180\n\nWhole area `road_km_impassable` 13.159 km vs 14.015 km.\n\nNo additional passability benefit on the expressway.\n\n### Conclusion on smallest set\n\nNo tested set within the 4-run budget achieves `road_km_impassable = 0` on the `Lekki-Epe Expressway`:\n\n* smallest 1-intervention set: city-wide new drainage 40 mm/h leaves 1.091 km impassable, max 0.405 m.\n* best tested 2-intervention set: city-wide `capacity_factor 3.0 + add_mm_h 40.0` leaves 0.617 km impassable, max 0.405 m.\n* adding `green in Lekki Phase 1` as 3rd intervention does not reduce expressway impassable km further.\n\nIf strict 0 km / <0.3 m passability is required, additional targeted work along the expressway corridor itself would need to be tested next.\n\nAll results are from the planning flood model, not a forecast.\n"
   }
